From: Antigravity Agent <antigravity@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] rmtfs: storage: add Xiaomi sagit OEM partition aliases

On Xiaomi Mi 6 (sagit) with Qualcomm MSM8998, the modem firmware requests
`/boot/modem_fsg_oem_1` and `/boot/modem_fsg_oem_2` via QMI remote storage.
Without these mappings, rmtfs rejects the requests with -EINVAL, causing
the modem DSP RTOS watchdog (dog_hb.c) to starve and crash.

Map both aliases to the factory "fsg" partition.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity Agent <antigravity@google.com>
---
 storage.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/storage.c
+++ b/storage.c
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@ static const struct partition partition_table[] = {
 	{ "/boot/modem_tunning", "modem_tunning", "tunning" },
 	{ "/boot/modem_tng", "modem_tng", "tunning" },
+	/* Xiaomi sagit OEM partitions */
+	{ "/boot/modem_fsg_oem_1", "modem_fsg_oem_1", "fsg" },
+	{ "/boot/modem_fsg_oem_2", "modem_fsg_oem_2", "fsg" },
 	/* OnePlus/Oppo OEM NV backup partitions */
 	{ "/oem/nvbk/static", "oem_stanvbk", "oem_stanvbk" },
 	{ "/oem/nvbk/dynamic", "oem_dycnvbk", "oem_dycnvbk" },
